  UP #2 (up-count 2) replies t+118.99 and         t+124.26 02:27:52 = t+121.0 box
                     t+121.09 -> t+121.09
  DOWN #2 (the host  3 failures ~ t+197           after    02:29:08 = t+197.0 box
  process exited                                  the
  at t+185)                                       sampler

  => STEP 6 PASS: all seven parameters are accepted and read back on both
     instances, and the three that are observable on the wire are OBEYED.
     `normal-interval 5` gives a measured 5.0-5.2 s period while Up.
     `critical-interval 2` is obeyed too, but the observed PERIOD while Down is
     4.1 s, not 2 s, because the period is timeout + interval; the
     discriminator is still sound, since had the instance stayed on the normal
     interval the period would have been timeout 2 + 5 = 7 s, and it was 4.1 s.
     `fail-count 3` and `up-count 2` put the instance Down and Up at times the
     DUT's own trigger log confirms to within ~1 s on all four transitions, across
     a 9 s offset between two instruments that do not share a clock. Throughout,
     the control instance kept polling and being answered, so none of this is an
     artefact of the measurement stopping.

